t received from a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous sequence. Typically, you use this to transform from one type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of element to another."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5"},{"type":"text","text":". The closure provided to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" and looks up a corresponding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"romanNumeralDict"},{"type":"text","text":" dictionary. This means the outer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterates over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" instances instead of the underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces. Also, the dictionary doesn’t provide a key for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4"},{"type":"text","text":", and the closure throws an error for any key it can’t look up, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receiving this value from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" ends the modified sequence with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeL